The classic! A few ways:

**Modern best practice — Flexbox:**
```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

**For horizontal centering only:**
```css
.child {
  margin: 0 auto;
}
/* (needs a defined width on the child) */
```

**Grid (cleanest for both axes):**
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
}
```

**Absolute positioning (if you must):**
```css
.child {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

Flexbox or Grid are the go-tos these days. Absolute positioning is mostly for legacy or specific overlay cases.
